WEBVTT

00:06.089 --> 00:08.258
THIS EPISODE CONTAINS
GRAPHIC DEPICTIONS OF SCHOOL VIOLENCE,

00:08.341 --> 00:09.884
WHICH SOME VIEWERS MAY FIND DISTURBING.

00:20.687 --> 00:22.063
Is this the person?

00:22.564 --> 00:24.566
Could you check out
the other addresses as well?

00:24.649 --> 00:25.859
Yes, just read them out.

00:27.027 --> 00:28.903
13-1 Seojung-ro.

00:28.987 --> 00:30.739
319-2 Changdong-ro.

00:30.822 --> 00:31.865
ORDERER ADDRESS LIST

00:31.948 --> 00:32.949
417-1 Sanggok-ro.

00:33.658 --> 00:35.035
27 Daewon 3-ro.

00:35.118 --> 00:36.327
21 Mijeong-ro.

00:38.121 --> 00:42.000
Oh. This person was identified
at all the addresses you just gave me.

00:47.672 --> 00:49.049
Officer Lee, it's me.

00:49.132 --> 00:51.843
I checked it out, and that guy
was at all the addresses you gave me.

00:52.635 --> 00:54.512
Okay, got it. Thanks.

01:18.828 --> 01:21.664
Come on, cheer up.
Aren't you happy to see me, huh?

01:54.739 --> 01:55.698
Everyone okay?

01:56.491 --> 01:57.492
You kids okay?

01:58.660 --> 01:59.619
You're not hurt?

01:59.702 --> 02:00.578
No.

02:01.246 --> 02:02.664
We… we seem to be fine.

02:03.790 --> 02:06.626
That's a relief. Get the students out
of the building right away.

02:06.709 --> 02:07.794
Yeah.

02:34.320 --> 02:35.488
Hey.

02:35.572 --> 02:36.781
Wait. Wait, wait, wait.

02:36.865 --> 02:39.742
G… Gyu-jin, man, I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

02:43.538 --> 02:44.873
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

02:47.375 --> 02:49.878
I'm sorry. I'm sorry, Gyu-jin.

02:53.715 --> 02:54.841
Hold on.

03:06.394 --> 03:08.104
I have no way of knowing…

03:11.065 --> 03:12.817
everything you've been through.

03:15.653 --> 03:17.739
Except what you're about to do…

03:21.993 --> 03:23.912
is only gonna hurt you in the end.

03:25.246 --> 03:27.040
Don't act like you understand me.

03:31.127 --> 03:32.212
It's too late.

03:33.213 --> 03:34.339
It isn't too late.

03:38.343 --> 03:40.762
If you can tell me how difficult

03:42.347 --> 03:43.848
things have been for you,

03:47.852 --> 03:49.729
then I'll be able to help you.

03:59.572 --> 04:01.741
I wanna hear what you've got to say.

04:05.245 --> 04:06.246
I mean that.

04:13.920 --> 04:15.129
But before anything,

04:16.673 --> 04:18.549
you need to put the gun down.

04:19.676 --> 04:21.177
And then we can talk.

04:25.598 --> 04:27.058
Think you can do that?

05:02.051 --> 05:03.052
That asshole…

05:07.473 --> 05:10.018
He's just a total piece of shit.

05:11.853 --> 05:13.146
Thank you for telling me.

05:14.397 --> 05:16.524
You took the high road, Gyu-jin.
Thank you.

05:24.949 --> 05:28.202
Thank you. You did so well.

05:30.079 --> 05:31.331
You did the right thing.

05:48.431 --> 05:50.141
Hey, my son is in there!

05:50.224 --> 05:51.184
I need to get in!

05:51.267 --> 05:52.352
How do I get in?

05:57.190 --> 05:58.274
Seong-jun!

05:58.358 --> 06:01.819
Oh my God, Seong-jun!
What happened?! Oh my God!

06:01.903 --> 06:05.948
Seong-jun, wake up! It's Mom!
I'm here! Please wake up! Look at me!

06:06.032 --> 06:09.494
What on earth happened in there,
for God's sake? Get your hands off me!

06:09.577 --> 06:11.412
I'm here! I'm here!

06:11.496 --> 06:13.247
Hey! Don't you touch me!

06:13.331 --> 06:15.958
Seong-jun! Seong-jun, it's me! Dad's here!

06:16.042 --> 06:17.627
God! God!

06:18.127 --> 06:20.004
Ma'am, don't push. You can't go inside.

06:20.088 --> 06:23.549
- What the hell happened?
- Everybody, stand back, please!

06:27.261 --> 06:29.931
Gyu-jin! Gyu-jin! Oh, sorry!

06:30.014 --> 06:31.891
I… No, I… I'm… No, I'm his mom.

06:31.974 --> 06:34.727
- I'm sorry, you can't see him.
- Hey, no! I'm his mom!

06:34.811 --> 06:36.771
- Gyu-jin! Hey! Let me go!
- I'm sorry.

06:36.854 --> 06:38.689
- You can't go over there.
- But I'm his mom!

06:38.773 --> 06:40.608
- I'm sorry.
- Gyu-jin! What's wrong?

06:40.691 --> 06:43.444
Why are you over there?
Gyu-jin, what's happening?

06:43.528 --> 06:44.737
Are you in trouble?

06:44.821 --> 06:46.823
Please tell me you didn't do this!

06:46.906 --> 06:48.741
Gyu-jin! No!

06:48.825 --> 06:50.451
Gyun-jin, no! No, no!

06:50.535 --> 06:53.121
Why are you getting into that police car?

06:53.204 --> 06:54.831
Gyu-jin!

06:55.373 --> 06:57.250
No! No!

06:57.333 --> 07:00.002
Gyu-jin!

07:04.924 --> 07:06.509
Detective Seo.

07:07.260 --> 07:08.136
Yeah, go ahead.

07:09.011 --> 07:10.346
Everything is set for the arrest.

07:10.430 --> 07:12.849
All detectives are in position.
Should we go for it?

07:12.932 --> 07:15.476
Tell everyone
to hold their positions for a bit.

07:37.081 --> 07:39.542
Don't worry,
I'll take you straight to Jeon Won-seong.

07:40.126 --> 07:41.002
Don't move.

07:42.378 --> 07:43.296
Hey!

07:45.715 --> 07:46.674
I caught him.

07:46.757 --> 07:48.217
Just a piece of paper

07:48.301 --> 07:49.802
and a bunch of bullets.

07:50.803 --> 07:52.722
Where is that list of addresses now?

07:54.056 --> 07:55.391
I think I threw it out.

07:56.350 --> 07:58.686
All the people who are getting those guns,

07:59.479 --> 08:00.480
maybe to all of them,

08:00.563 --> 08:03.357
a gun actually could equal
justice and power.

08:03.941 --> 08:06.569
Right there.
There's a high school kid on that list.

08:07.236 --> 08:08.696
Shouldn't we go check?

08:08.779 --> 08:11.449
Kids have to turn their phones in
before class.

08:13.868 --> 08:16.496
GYEONGIN SEOBU POLICE STATION
DETECTIVE SEO

08:16.579 --> 08:19.332
ONCE THE SITUATION IS OVER,
ARREST MOON BAEK

08:20.541 --> 08:21.959
Do, everyone's ready.

08:22.752 --> 08:23.753
Should we get him?

08:26.464 --> 08:28.007
All right, everyone. We're going now.

08:28.090 --> 08:29.133
Copy that.

08:30.009 --> 08:31.677
Team two, move! Team two, move!

08:40.520 --> 08:42.188
Huh? What?

08:42.271 --> 08:44.649
Where did he go?

08:44.732 --> 08:46.192
Where did that bastard go?

08:47.568 --> 08:49.529
- Did you see him?
- No, we didn't.

08:49.612 --> 08:51.697
All right, block the main gates
and side exits.

08:51.781 --> 08:52.615
Okay.

08:52.698 --> 08:54.325
- Secure the exits!
- This way!

08:54.408 --> 08:55.368
You three! Over here!

08:59.288 --> 09:00.414
Officer Lee.

09:01.290 --> 09:03.125
I just received
some background information

09:03.209 --> 09:05.127
on Moon Baek from Dongwol Industries.

09:05.211 --> 09:06.796
But he isn't the guy we met.

09:56.762 --> 09:58.681
ORDERER ADDRESS LIST

09:58.764 --> 09:59.765
LEE DO

10:41.265 --> 10:43.934
Unfortunately,
South Korea can no longer be called

10:44.018 --> 10:45.061
a gun-free country.

10:45.144 --> 10:49.023
Citizens are becoming increasingly anxious
as deadly shootings continue to occur.

10:49.106 --> 10:50.983
A mass shooting occurred
at a local high school.

10:51.067 --> 10:53.069
The shooting follows two recent incidents,

10:53.152 --> 10:56.280
one of which took place at a gosiwon
and another at a police station.

10:56.364 --> 10:58.783
Earlier,
a convenience store in Gyeonggi Province

10:58.866 --> 11:00.534
was robbed at gunpoint.

11:00.618 --> 11:03.245
The incident took place
at approximately 2:00 a.m. at the store…

11:03.329 --> 11:06.499
Although opinions vary
with regard to the source of the guns,

11:06.582 --> 11:07.792
as well as who may be behind…

11:07.875 --> 11:10.252
Citizens call on
the government to take action

11:10.336 --> 11:11.712
against the rash of mass shootings.

11:11.796 --> 11:15.132
- Where are the guns coming from?
- Do you know who's behind it?

11:15.216 --> 11:17.593
- What safety measures…
- Commissioner.

11:17.677 --> 11:19.553
How many more shootings will there be?

11:19.637 --> 11:23.224
There are more guns, right?
People are paralyzed with fear.

11:23.307 --> 11:26.519
So are there more guns out there or not?

11:26.602 --> 11:28.562
Or are you in the dark about that as well?

11:28.646 --> 11:30.940
Speculation and conjecture aren't helpful.

11:31.023 --> 11:33.693
You will just have to trust the police
and be patient.

11:39.115 --> 11:40.616
Hey. He's coming. He's coming.

11:40.700 --> 11:42.618
- Sir.
- Sir.

11:45.204 --> 11:47.581
I got a call from the police
earlier today.

11:47.665 --> 11:50.793
Listen. I know that we're not exactly
law-abiding fellows at this table,

11:50.876 --> 11:53.754
but if you wanna continue
making your living here in South Korea,

11:53.838 --> 11:57.299
then there's one thing that you must
never, ever get involved in.

11:57.967 --> 11:59.468
And that is guns.

11:59.552 --> 12:01.178
Don't you think it's a good thing?

12:01.262 --> 12:04.932
I mean no disrespect, sir,
but how long can we go on like this?

12:05.015 --> 12:07.727
Shouldn't we be moving away from knives?
Join the rest of the world?

12:07.810 --> 12:11.605
Assault, fraud, murder, drugs.
All of those crimes are settled in court.

12:13.232 --> 12:14.316
But guns aren't.

12:15.401 --> 12:16.819
Because then it's a military issue.

12:16.902 --> 12:18.779
Exactly.

12:18.863 --> 12:22.199
The second we get our hands on guns,
they'll put us down like dogs.

12:25.453 --> 12:27.288
Oh shit, man.

12:27.371 --> 12:29.999
One wrong move
and those guys'll want my ass.

12:30.499 --> 12:33.753
So what should we do
with all those guns in storage?

12:49.059 --> 12:49.894
Hey.

12:52.062 --> 12:54.106
Call that cop I hate, would you?

12:54.190 --> 12:55.357
Yes, boss.

12:55.441 --> 12:57.443
Are you kidding me?!

12:57.526 --> 13:00.070
You were all at the scene,
yet you failed to apprehend one guy?

13:00.154 --> 13:01.947
Have you all gone blind or something?

13:02.031 --> 13:05.117
I want you to do whatever it takes to find
that bastard and bring him in here.

13:05.201 --> 13:07.995
I don't care how many addresses,
you better collect all those guns.

13:08.078 --> 13:09.497
One more shooting

13:09.580 --> 13:12.458
and all of us will be turning in
our badges. Do you understand me?

13:12.541 --> 13:14.168
Have I made myself clear?

13:14.668 --> 13:15.836
Yes, sir.

13:22.510 --> 13:23.344
Lee Do,

13:23.427 --> 13:25.346
you're back to work starting today.

13:25.429 --> 13:28.182
I'll deal with the paperwork.
Now go join the rest of the team.

13:31.268 --> 13:32.561
GONG SEOK-HO

13:42.363 --> 13:45.282
God dammit. He seems eager, doesn't he?

13:56.794 --> 13:57.628
Here.

14:00.381 --> 14:01.924
This is an actual gun.

14:02.007 --> 14:04.677
You come any closer and I'll shoot.
I'll do it.

14:07.471 --> 14:08.514
Shit, don't shoot!

14:08.597 --> 14:09.431
Don't shoot!

14:15.104 --> 14:17.606
Where'd you get this gun?

14:20.526 --> 14:21.694
Ah, jeez.

14:21.777 --> 14:24.738
I bought a club
from this meth dealer I know. Mr. Kim.

14:24.822 --> 14:26.699
He sold it to me real cheap.

14:26.782 --> 14:29.451
And I just happened to find these
in the storage room.

14:30.286 --> 14:32.121
And where is this Mr. Kim now?

14:33.289 --> 14:35.708
I have no clue! How the hell would I know?

14:35.791 --> 14:38.961
When I found them, I thought,
"Oh, is this guy trying to screw me over?"

14:39.044 --> 14:40.170
I wanted to end him myself.

14:40.254 --> 14:42.256
But, god dammit,
I got no clue where he is.

14:44.300 --> 14:46.760
- Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait!
- You expect me to believe that?

14:46.844 --> 14:49.597
Ow! Okay, okay, okay, just wait!
Hey, hey. Hold on a minute.

14:49.680 --> 14:51.390
Here, just look at this.

14:55.311 --> 14:57.187
Ow! Shit, man!

14:57.938 --> 15:02.192
Look. I've got a guy named Gu Jeong-man.
He works for me, does my clean-up jobs.

15:03.027 --> 15:06.655
Well, it just so happens that the guy
you're looking for is part of his crew.

15:08.282 --> 15:10.659
And I've got no clue how he knew.

15:10.743 --> 15:12.453
But he was loitering
near the storage room,

15:12.536 --> 15:14.204
exactly where the guns were.

15:15.164 --> 15:16.415
So what does it mean?

15:16.498 --> 15:19.043
All those bastards are
looking for guns right now.

15:19.126 --> 15:20.794
You get it? Make sense?

15:26.175 --> 15:29.094
So why are you showing me
all your cards and coming clean?

15:29.678 --> 15:32.723
Because I couldn't believe
there were guns and I didn't know!

15:34.058 --> 15:35.601
If I'm about to get myself shot,

15:35.684 --> 15:37.728
then I'm not gonna sit around
and do nothing.

15:39.146 --> 15:41.357
I'm willing to cooperate with you
on everything,

15:41.440 --> 15:45.611
as long as you keep me and my club
out of this little situation, Officer Lee.

15:46.362 --> 15:48.405
I would never mess around with guns.

15:49.281 --> 15:51.241
I'm just an innocent bystander.

15:52.660 --> 15:53.786
Okay?

15:56.246 --> 15:59.124
Come on. You already took them all
the last time you were here.

15:59.625 --> 16:01.335
- Who did?
- The police?

16:02.586 --> 16:04.588
They showed me their badges.
I turned the guns over.

16:04.672 --> 16:06.131
So why are you here again?

16:06.924 --> 16:08.050
- Hey.
- What?

16:08.550 --> 16:10.803
Would anyone other than us
have come by here?

16:10.886 --> 16:13.347
No, we're the ones in charge of this area.

16:13.430 --> 16:15.099
I did my part,
so figure it out yourselves.

16:15.182 --> 16:16.558
Okay. Well, could we just--

16:17.267 --> 16:19.311
- Sir, we've never been here before.
- I already did.

16:19.395 --> 16:21.605
- So I just have to ask you.
- Come on, I did. Hey, no way!

16:21.689 --> 16:23.983
This is ridiculous. Man…

16:24.066 --> 16:27.194
Your people already took it.
Why are you asking for it again?

16:27.277 --> 16:28.988
This is very serious, sir.
If you're lying,

16:29.071 --> 16:31.156
you'll be in a lot of trouble.
Just give us the gun.

16:31.240 --> 16:33.784
Man! You police are unreal, you know?
That's it. I'm done.

16:33.867 --> 16:36.328
Hang on, sir. Just wait.
You never gave us any gun, sir.

16:36.412 --> 16:37.538
Sir! Wait a minute! Just--

16:41.250 --> 16:43.961
So how many guns have you found?

16:44.044 --> 16:47.464
We've collected guns from about half
the addresses on the lists we have.

16:47.548 --> 16:49.174
Only half? What are you gonna do

16:49.258 --> 16:51.885
if a madman starts shooting up
some place tomorrow?

16:51.969 --> 16:55.014
I'm sorry, sir.
I have every officer trying to find them

16:55.097 --> 16:56.098
as quickly as possible.

16:56.181 --> 16:57.891
What about those lowlifes
trying to get guns

16:57.975 --> 16:59.351
by impersonating the police?

16:59.435 --> 17:01.812
- Yes, we're addressing that as well.
- Right.

17:02.312 --> 17:04.273
Starting today,
the Joint Investigation Office

17:04.356 --> 17:05.607
will be handling this case.

17:05.691 --> 17:07.651
Transfer your investigative materials
over to them,

17:07.735 --> 17:08.944
and stay out of it from now on.

17:09.028 --> 17:09.903
Please, Commissioner.

17:16.160 --> 17:18.495
JOINT INVESTIGATION HQ

17:21.832 --> 17:23.667
The Ministry of Health and Welfare

17:23.751 --> 17:26.128
issued a manual on how to treat
victims of mass shootings

17:26.211 --> 17:28.839
at several key hospitals
around the region.

17:28.922 --> 17:30.049
As a result, the medical…

17:30.716 --> 17:32.217
Ugh! Bread.

17:32.301 --> 17:35.220
Doesn't she know I get heartburn
when she brings flour-based things?

17:35.304 --> 17:38.348
God, could she be
any more thickheaded and oblivious?

17:38.432 --> 17:39.892
If she was able to get herself a job

17:39.975 --> 17:42.352
after graduating from
some backwoods dump of a college,

17:42.436 --> 17:44.188
she should at least be able to buy lunch.

17:44.271 --> 17:45.564
Right? God!

17:45.647 --> 17:48.275
How many times do we have to repeat
something before she understands?

17:48.358 --> 17:50.736
It's like she wants everyone to know
she went to a bad school.

17:50.819 --> 17:51.653
Mm-hmm.

17:52.154 --> 17:53.447
I know you're busy,

17:53.530 --> 17:55.449
so I'll order your fave later.
Mango bingsu.

17:55.532 --> 17:56.867
Aw, you're the best.

17:59.620 --> 18:01.705
I'm going to work out
with a personal trainer

18:01.789 --> 18:02.664
starting next week,

18:02.748 --> 18:05.000
so would you mind
taking me off night shifts for a while?

18:05.084 --> 18:07.169
You hardly did
any night shifts last month.

18:07.252 --> 18:09.463
Aw, come on.
You're the head nurse. Please?

18:09.546 --> 18:11.882
Oh dear. All right, it's okay.

18:11.965 --> 18:14.009
I'll make adjustments to the schedule.

18:14.093 --> 18:16.512
At least we've got someone else
who can take those shifts.

18:17.179 --> 18:19.973
Oh, thank you so much!

18:20.057 --> 18:22.684
I'll go ahead
and order that bingsu right away.

18:24.103 --> 18:27.523
I've been hearing about people who are
scrambling to buy look-alike firearms

18:27.606 --> 18:29.942
or even gun parts
from foreign retailers online.

18:30.025 --> 18:32.194
I think we need to start
having frank discussions

18:32.277 --> 18:33.946
about legalizing gun ownership.

18:34.446 --> 18:35.280
What do you mean?

18:35.823 --> 18:39.034
You actually think we should be
legalizing guns here in South Korea,

18:39.118 --> 18:41.120
one of the safest countries in the world?

18:41.203 --> 18:43.872
What I'm saying is that
instead of banning gun ownership outright,

18:43.956 --> 18:45.916
we need to legislate it,
institutionalize it--

18:45.999 --> 18:48.293
Well, this certainly isn't something
we can resolve today.

18:48.377 --> 18:50.212
And now, since we are in the midst

18:50.295 --> 18:52.339
of an unprecedented slew
of mass shootings,

18:52.422 --> 18:55.926
I want to ask any of our viewers who might
currently be in possession of a firearm

18:56.009 --> 18:58.137
to please report it
to your nearest police station

18:58.220 --> 18:59.263
as soon as possible.

19:03.642 --> 19:06.019
So it looks like
Gong Seok-ho has been cooperating

19:06.103 --> 19:07.646
with the police investigation.

19:10.482 --> 19:13.360
The guns that we couriered
are in transit now.

19:13.443 --> 19:16.363
We also confirmed the guns
have been used in other neighborhoods.

19:16.446 --> 19:18.407
And what's Gu Jeong-man doing now?

19:18.490 --> 19:22.244
Looks like he's only been able to collect
about half of the guns we distributed.

19:23.162 --> 19:24.246
Half of them?

19:26.999 --> 19:30.377
Aw. Someone should be coming out
with a bang right about now.

19:30.460 --> 19:33.797
We put all those guns out
for people to use.

19:34.548 --> 19:37.885
So where are all the street shootouts
or police showdowns?

19:39.178 --> 19:41.722
Come on, guys.
Somebody do something already.

19:49.646 --> 19:50.522
Nice, huh?

19:50.606 --> 19:52.107
Hey, this isn't a toy, asshole.

19:52.191 --> 19:55.068
I said this isn't a toy, you dumbass.
Stop fooling around.

19:57.738 --> 20:00.532
- Oh yeah! Sweet.
- Do your military service?

20:01.950 --> 20:03.869
- This one's mine!
- Say that again, jerk.

20:03.952 --> 20:05.579
You moron.

20:05.662 --> 20:08.582
Bang, bang, bang! Bang, bang, bang!

20:08.665 --> 20:10.918
Wait, that's not it?

20:11.001 --> 20:13.712
Hey, man,
do not make me repeat myself again.

20:13.795 --> 20:17.424
Hey, do you have trust issues
or something? Huh?

20:17.925 --> 20:22.262
I already told you. We are
the best money launderers in town, yeah.

20:22.346 --> 20:23.805
So you want goods?

20:23.889 --> 20:26.683
Man, don't you know
that goods equals cash?

20:26.767 --> 20:29.394
We launder it all, and we don't care
if the money's a little sketchy,

20:29.478 --> 20:33.523
somewhat shady, or downright illegal.
So stop worrying and send it over, okay?

20:37.945 --> 20:39.071
Jeez.

20:40.822 --> 20:43.033
Whoa, sir, is that a cigar you've got?

20:43.116 --> 20:44.576
Yeah, this was a gift.

20:45.827 --> 20:48.080
Apparently, cigars are a symbol
of status and style.

20:48.163 --> 20:50.374
All the way from Cuba.

20:50.457 --> 20:51.458
What do you think?

20:54.044 --> 20:56.255
- Cool, huh?
- You look super cool.

20:56.880 --> 20:58.799
Here.

20:58.882 --> 21:00.133
Want a drag?

21:08.558 --> 21:09.851
God, you lame-ass.

21:09.935 --> 21:12.479
You're not supposed to inhale cigar smoke.
Give it back.

21:12.562 --> 21:13.772
Here you are.

21:15.774 --> 21:19.486
Jeong-man, we gotta clean you up.
You're looking rough around the edges.

21:19.569 --> 21:20.654
Oh, by the way,

21:21.530 --> 21:23.740
I've got a big job coming up,
and it's gonna be tough,

21:23.824 --> 21:25.659
so I'm gonna need you to work this one.

21:27.160 --> 21:28.787
What kind of big job is it?

21:34.126 --> 21:36.295
I'm gonna take over
all of Mr. Kim's businesses.

21:36.378 --> 21:37.337
What?

21:39.548 --> 21:41.133
- Mr. Kim, the one--
- Yup, Mr. Kim.

21:41.216 --> 21:42.968
The one you and I both know well.

21:43.677 --> 21:45.387
We need to clean all this up now.

21:45.470 --> 21:48.640
Did you know Mr. Kim was selling
something incredible he got from overseas,

21:48.724 --> 21:50.600
and apparently,
it's a total fucking cash cow?

21:50.684 --> 21:52.936
- You hear me?
- Yeah, but all of Mr. Kim's businesses?

21:53.020 --> 21:54.563
- That seems too big for us.
- Ah-ah.

21:54.646 --> 21:58.025
My orders came straight from the top.
Now we just need to take care of Mr. Kim.

21:58.650 --> 22:01.361
And aren't you the expert in that area,
Jeong-man?

22:02.863 --> 22:03.989
Sir, I was thinking

22:04.698 --> 22:06.366
that once this job is done

22:06.950 --> 22:08.493
that maybe you could give

22:09.411 --> 22:11.747
me and the boys
one of our own businesses to run.

22:14.583 --> 22:15.584
Hey.

22:16.668 --> 22:18.795
Have some faith in me, would you?

22:19.880 --> 22:20.797
If this job goes well,

22:20.881 --> 22:22.883
don't you think
I'll give you at least one?

22:24.134 --> 22:25.344
So are you in or not?

22:26.553 --> 22:28.638
I'm in. Yes, I… I'll do it.

22:28.722 --> 22:30.265
That's my guy!

22:30.349 --> 22:32.351
My Jeong-man!

22:33.101 --> 22:35.937
You know,
you're the only one that I can trust.

22:36.730 --> 22:38.273
Hey, give me those.

22:51.453 --> 22:54.373
Come on, hyeong.
What are you waiting for?

22:55.207 --> 22:58.001
We've got guns now,
so let's go kill those fuckers.

22:59.544 --> 23:00.629
You know something?

23:01.380 --> 23:04.424
A lion waits for the perfect time to kill,
even if its prey is small.

23:05.425 --> 23:06.927
Not because it's weak, but

23:07.636 --> 23:09.679
'cause it doesn't wanna make a mistake.

23:11.515 --> 23:12.974
And when the time is right,

23:14.017 --> 23:15.936
then we need to do it all at once.

23:16.853 --> 23:19.773
How many times do I have to tell you?

23:19.856 --> 23:22.234
Gu Jeong-man knows where Mr. Kim is.

23:22.317 --> 23:25.695
- Are you sure?
- Am I sure? Jesus, what…

23:30.575 --> 23:31.660
If you don't believe me,

23:31.743 --> 23:34.329
then why don't you go ask
Gu Jeong-man yourself?

23:36.373 --> 23:37.707
Mr. Kim had all of these guns?

23:38.417 --> 23:39.334
Yes.

23:40.043 --> 23:42.796
Then Mr. Kim is responsible
for distributing all the guns

23:42.879 --> 23:44.339
used in the shootings so far?

23:44.423 --> 23:46.925
- By hiding them in parcels?
- Yes, that's correct.

23:48.510 --> 23:50.387
Where is this Kim bastard now?

23:50.470 --> 23:52.722
We're currently unable
to locate Mr. Kim, sir.

23:53.598 --> 23:56.726
If we use Gu Jeong-man
and Mr. Gong to find Mr. Kim for us,

23:57.477 --> 24:01.481
then we'll be able to find the real people
who are distributing the guns.

24:01.565 --> 24:04.025
All right. Come up with a plan for it,

24:04.109 --> 24:07.279
and then keep Joint Investigations updated
on how it's all going.

24:07.362 --> 24:09.030
Yes, sir.

24:09.114 --> 24:09.990
DOCUMENT FOR APPROVAL

24:10.073 --> 24:11.241
I need your signature.

24:15.328 --> 24:16.288
Hey.

24:16.872 --> 24:18.832
Didn't I tell you
to stay out of this case?

24:18.915 --> 24:22.586
Commissioner, these guns are
continuing to pop up all over the city.

24:22.669 --> 24:25.046
Gunfire is ringing across Seoul
every minute.

24:25.130 --> 24:27.340
Three incidents have been reported
already today.

24:27.924 --> 24:29.718
We have to find those guns
as soon as we can.

24:29.801 --> 24:31.845
We need to cut them off at the pass.

24:39.769 --> 24:41.062
BACKGROUND CHECK REPORT

24:41.146 --> 24:44.357
Officer Lee Do found the man responsible
for the illegal distribution of the guns.

24:44.441 --> 24:47.777
Commissioner, we need you to put
all your focus on locating this man.

24:47.861 --> 24:52.240
And meanwhile, we're going to try to find
as many of those guns as we possibly can

24:53.283 --> 24:54.951
and hopefully get a lead on him.

24:59.956 --> 25:03.210
An announcement from HQ.
All officers must be on emergency alert.

25:03.293 --> 25:06.755
We now have a lead on suspects
impersonating police to obtain firearms.

25:06.838 --> 25:09.424
Please collect all firearms
at the listed addresses.

25:09.925 --> 25:14.095
I repeat, all officers must be
on emergency alert today. We now…

25:15.013 --> 25:16.014
MY DAUGHTER

25:20.268 --> 25:23.146
The person you are calling is unavailable.

25:23.230 --> 25:24.814
Please try again later.

25:25.774 --> 25:28.360
What do you mean,
you don't have it? That's insane!

25:28.443 --> 25:31.988
Hey, don't you…
don't you dare put your hands on me!

25:32.072 --> 25:35.200
- Yeah, that's right. You can go to hell!
- I want my money back now!

25:35.283 --> 25:37.244
- Back off!
- Don't you…

25:37.327 --> 25:38.662
Dad, I was wondering.

25:38.745 --> 25:40.664
Do you think
you could help me out a little bit?

25:41.164 --> 25:42.999
Huh? Why?

25:43.750 --> 25:46.795
Your pension. Do you think
you could maybe get an advance?

25:48.046 --> 25:50.382
Oh, have you completely lost it this time?

25:50.465 --> 25:53.260
- Now you're just trying to butter me up.
- I'm serious, Dad. Can you help?

25:53.343 --> 25:54.761
- I don't have it.
- Excuse me.

25:54.844 --> 25:57.305
- So file a report with the police!
- Sir, could you…

25:57.389 --> 25:58.932
- Sir, could you help me?
- What?

25:59.015 --> 26:00.559
Sir, please, I need my money.

26:00.642 --> 26:02.394
Without it, I'm totally done for.

26:02.477 --> 26:05.397
Please have some mercy for me, sir.
I'm begging you, please.

26:05.480 --> 26:06.815
- Please.
- Let go, damn it!

26:06.898 --> 26:09.568
My dad worked for his pension
all his life.

26:09.651 --> 26:12.279
- That money's all he had.
- Go ahead and sue us. Now get out! Jeez.

26:12.362 --> 26:14.906
Please have some mercy on us.

26:14.990 --> 26:16.199
Please, sir!

26:58.408 --> 27:00.118
Hey! Mr. Gong is here.

27:00.785 --> 27:03.371
- What the hell's he doing here?!
- Hide the fucking guns!

27:03.455 --> 27:06.249
- Oh shit! Come on!
- Hey. Come on! Hurry up, hurry up!

27:06.333 --> 27:07.375
We're fucked, man!

27:07.459 --> 27:10.712
- Come on, move! Quickly! Come on.
- Hurry, hurry! Go, go, go!

27:21.389 --> 27:22.390
Hey.

27:27.520 --> 27:31.066
Hey! Jeong-man, what's up?

27:31.608 --> 27:32.442
Hello, sir.

27:34.361 --> 27:35.445
What's with the vibe?

27:38.990 --> 27:41.910
What were you all doing,
and why so out of breath?

27:42.535 --> 27:43.495
What?

27:44.579 --> 27:46.539
Oh, well, we were all just cleaning up.

27:47.666 --> 27:49.542
Ah!

27:49.626 --> 27:52.587
Oh, hey. You can't expect too much
from these old buildings.

27:52.671 --> 27:53.672
Live and let live.

27:56.966 --> 27:58.885
We've never met before, have we, boys?

27:59.427 --> 28:00.553
Hello, sir.

28:00.637 --> 28:01.805
Nice to meet you.

28:02.305 --> 28:03.556
Have a seat, sir.

28:07.143 --> 28:09.479
I spotted a really good bakery
on the way here.

28:10.021 --> 28:11.022
That's nice.

28:15.777 --> 28:16.653
Right.

28:17.862 --> 28:18.697
Thank you, sir.

28:18.780 --> 28:21.533
Remember when you asked me
if I knew your boys' names?

28:22.242 --> 28:23.076
What?

28:23.159 --> 28:24.828
Well, I felt really bad about it,

28:24.911 --> 28:27.747
and I just assumed
there would be about 20 of them.

28:27.831 --> 28:30.291
That should be enough to share,
shouldn't it?

28:31.292 --> 28:33.586
Yes. This is more than enough.

28:34.671 --> 28:36.089
Pass these around and share them.

28:37.298 --> 28:38.258
Jeong-man.

28:40.885 --> 28:41.970
Can we have a talk?

28:45.098 --> 28:46.516
Give us a minute, would you?

28:48.059 --> 28:49.561
Thank you for the bread.

28:49.644 --> 28:52.355
Of course! You're welcome!

29:12.083 --> 29:13.084
Jeong-man.

29:13.960 --> 29:14.794
Yeah?

29:15.712 --> 29:17.964
How do you think
Mr. Kim's doing these days?

29:19.549 --> 29:20.467
I miss that guy.

29:21.468 --> 29:24.095
He's still buried deep down
in the hole that you dug, right?

29:26.431 --> 29:28.600
Why are you asking about Mr. Kim
all of a sudden?

29:28.683 --> 29:30.810
You know better than anyone how he is.

29:32.020 --> 29:32.937
You're right.

29:35.565 --> 29:36.566
I do.

29:50.079 --> 29:51.456
Ta-da!

29:52.540 --> 29:54.834
This is Mr. Kim's cell phone.

29:54.918 --> 29:59.172
Those stupid morons brought me his phone
but didn't remember to get the password.

29:59.255 --> 30:01.633
This phone has
all of his clients' numbers.

30:02.133 --> 30:04.511
Except I can't get any cash from them
without access.

30:04.594 --> 30:06.429
Oh, well…

30:06.513 --> 30:08.097
I don't know the password either.

30:08.181 --> 30:09.432
I know.

30:10.892 --> 30:14.145
But you, Jeong-man, have a way
to unlock this phone, don't you?

30:15.480 --> 30:16.397
Me?

30:24.322 --> 30:27.158
Cut off all of Mr. Kim's fingers
and bring them to me.

30:28.326 --> 30:30.328
Since you know where his body is.

30:33.790 --> 30:35.542
The sooner, the better. You get me?

30:37.460 --> 30:40.004
You know,
before his fingerprints rot away.

30:44.843 --> 30:47.303
Hey. So I went to suss him out a bit,

30:47.387 --> 30:49.973
and it looks like Gu Jeong-man's
definitely hiding Mr. Kim.

30:50.473 --> 30:53.101
I told him to come by the club tomorrow,
so you'd better be ready.

30:53.685 --> 30:56.729
And don't forget to leave my name
out of this, you get me?

30:59.607 --> 31:01.150
Shithead.

31:01.234 --> 31:02.235
Jesus.

31:09.909 --> 31:10.994
Hey, Jeong-man.

31:11.494 --> 31:13.663
So tell me. What'd Mr. Gong say?

31:14.163 --> 31:15.164
Huh?

31:18.376 --> 31:20.044
Why are you staring at me?
Just spit it out.

31:26.926 --> 31:28.344
Mr. Kim, do you trust me?

31:29.012 --> 31:30.972
Hey, what kind of question is that?

31:31.055 --> 31:33.349
Of course I do.
Now, what did that bastard say?

31:34.767 --> 31:36.936
He wants me to cut off
all of your fingers,

31:37.687 --> 31:39.105
and then bring them to him.

32:12.138 --> 32:12.972
Let's go.

32:13.056 --> 32:16.017
All right, let's go.

32:26.903 --> 32:28.905
My neck.

32:40.249 --> 32:41.125
Yes, boss.

32:42.001 --> 32:44.796
Gu Jeong-man showed up
to get Mr. Kim's fingers.

32:48.299 --> 32:50.093
Okay.

32:50.176 --> 32:51.511
Keep a close eye on him.

32:52.220 --> 32:53.262
Yes, I'm on it.

32:55.682 --> 32:56.808
Jeez!

32:56.891 --> 32:59.852
If you get buried out there,
no one will ever find your body.

33:02.021 --> 33:04.565
Apparently,
they're looking for Mr. Kim's fingers.

33:20.581 --> 33:22.417
What are all those morons doing?

33:22.500 --> 33:24.293
I've got no clue.

33:25.420 --> 33:26.421
Sir,

33:26.921 --> 33:29.298
why do you seem so worried
about Gu Jeong-man?

33:32.135 --> 33:33.469
If he bugs you that much,

33:33.553 --> 33:35.513
I can just take care of him quietly.

33:37.348 --> 33:38.182
Yeah?

33:41.728 --> 33:44.355
You don't know what Gu Jeong-man's
real strength is, do you?

33:44.439 --> 33:46.524
Please. That fucker's got no strengths.

33:46.607 --> 33:51.154
Gu Jeong-man cares so much about his boys.

33:56.451 --> 33:58.036
Give it back.

33:58.119 --> 34:00.580
Never mind.
You can keep your cheap smokes.

34:01.080 --> 34:02.915
- Let's see the photo, then.
- Sure.

34:07.670 --> 34:09.047
Wow!

34:09.130 --> 34:10.465
Wonderful.

34:10.548 --> 34:13.426
No one can do a clean-up quite like you,
my friend.

34:15.094 --> 34:18.848
You must have a pretty strong stomach.
Here you go. For your trouble.

34:18.931 --> 34:21.768
Thank you.
I mean, I do what I can to make money.

34:21.851 --> 34:23.686
I've got all those boys to take care of.

34:23.770 --> 34:26.564
Even though he's been doing this
for over a decade,

34:26.647 --> 34:29.233
his group of guys keeps getting bigger,
not smaller.

34:29.317 --> 34:32.320
Yeah, but they're just a bunch
of scrawny little gofers, aren't they?

34:35.323 --> 34:37.450
That's the most brilliant thing about it.

34:38.284 --> 34:40.995
Do you know anything about
those scrawny little gofers?

34:42.080 --> 34:44.540
People with guns are roaming the streets.

34:45.083 --> 34:47.335
Would you be able to fend off someone
you don't recognize

34:47.418 --> 34:48.836
and whose name you don't know?

34:49.629 --> 34:51.297
When they come at you with a gun?

34:53.007 --> 34:53.925
That's why

34:55.301 --> 34:58.387
the best option is to use that cop
to get rid of Gu Jeong-man.

35:00.139 --> 35:03.142
But what if he confesses
everything he did for you to the police?

35:03.226 --> 35:04.102
What?

35:04.602 --> 35:06.479
Did I say I'd turn him over alive?

35:09.482 --> 35:10.483
Just watch.

35:12.110 --> 35:13.611
This is my best plan yet.

35:18.991 --> 35:21.202
Come on, hurry up.

35:21.285 --> 35:23.121
- You load it all up?
- Yeah.

35:23.204 --> 35:25.706
I think that's everything. Come on.

35:34.298 --> 35:36.843
It's me. Gu Jeong-man's crew
was digging all morning,

35:36.926 --> 35:38.719
and now they're on the move again.

36:01.868 --> 36:03.202
Yes, boss.

36:05.788 --> 36:07.957
Those assholes just showed up
at the public bath.

36:08.541 --> 36:09.709
The public bath?

36:11.627 --> 36:15.506
That's their little routine,
taking a bath after they dig.

36:15.590 --> 36:17.842
Keep an eye on them
until Gu Jeong-man leaves,

36:17.925 --> 36:19.135
then head to his office.

36:19.719 --> 36:21.053
I'll join you when I'm done here.

36:25.349 --> 36:28.019
Why, you shit-eating bastards. Hey!

36:28.853 --> 36:30.021
Get out now!

36:38.112 --> 36:41.032
You guys are
just a bunch of fucking idiots.

36:41.782 --> 36:44.994
Hey!
Mr. Gong is waiting for Mr. Kim's fingers.

36:45.077 --> 36:46.621
Hurry up and go see him.

36:48.080 --> 36:49.081
Jeong-man.

36:50.666 --> 36:52.501
Turn that hot water up high.

37:00.676 --> 37:02.303
Hey, get out of the way, dumbass.

37:02.386 --> 37:04.347
I'm trying to get a good look
at his thing.

37:05.056 --> 37:07.892
Wow, his thing is as tiny as shit.

37:07.975 --> 37:10.728
What a fucking loser!

37:23.282 --> 37:24.492
YAKAM TOURIST HOTEL

37:24.575 --> 37:27.286
What the hell is taking
those guys so long?

37:28.454 --> 37:31.249
I don't know. But this doesn't look like
a public bath house.

37:31.332 --> 37:34.001
Are these assholes just messing with us?

37:34.085 --> 37:35.002
Shit.

37:36.254 --> 37:37.380
That's Gu Jeong-man!

37:45.263 --> 37:48.766
Detective Seo,
Gu Jeong-man is heading to the club now.

38:01.070 --> 38:03.864
GU JEONG-MAN
I'M ON MY WAY WITH MR. KIM'S FINGERS

38:08.119 --> 38:08.953
He's here.

38:09.036 --> 38:11.789
Everyone, check your firearms
and bulletproof vests.

38:11.872 --> 38:14.458
A shooting may occur, so be on high alert.

38:21.424 --> 38:23.134
Okay, be on your guard.

38:40.276 --> 38:42.320
Well! Come on in.

38:53.497 --> 38:54.582
What is it?

38:57.084 --> 38:58.502
I bet you're surprised.

38:59.378 --> 39:00.838
Gong, you stupid fucking bitch.

39:02.006 --> 39:04.050
You wanted these guys, right? Huh?

39:08.721 --> 39:09.722
So

39:11.057 --> 39:12.808
are you still gonna cut off my fingers?

39:13.476 --> 39:14.477
No.

39:16.312 --> 39:17.813
I don't use knives.

39:18.773 --> 39:19.607
Now what?

39:20.608 --> 39:23.110
Why don't you bring him
all your fingers yourself?

39:24.195 --> 39:25.571
I'll even give you a gun.

39:33.746 --> 39:35.664
Gu Jeong-man, that motherfucker…

39:40.711 --> 39:42.088
Shit! The fuck was that?!

39:43.798 --> 39:44.715
Hey.

39:48.177 --> 39:49.553
How do you like this thing?

39:50.513 --> 39:51.680
Huge, right?
